## 732, six conversions

a / а: 10^2=100 -> lg100=2; 100>0.
b / б: 10^7=10000000 -> lg10000000=7; seven zeroes, positive.
c / в: 10^-3=0.001 -> lg0.001=-3; positive.
d / г: 10^-6=0.000001 -> lg0.000001=-6; positive.
e / д: 10^(1/2)=sqrt10 -> lg(sqrt10)=1/2; positive.
f / е: 10^2.5=100sqrt10 -> lg(100sqrt10)=5/2=2.5; positive.
Each equivalence follows directly from the definition; no original numeral or exponent is altered.

## 733, nine literal identity proofs

a / а: 1000=10^3>0 -> lg1000=3.
b / б: 100000=10^5>0 -> lg100000=5.
c / в: 1/10000=10^-4>0 -> lg(1/10000)=-4.
d / г: cube-root10=10^(1/3)>0 -> lg(cube-root10)=1/3.
e / д: sqrt0.1=(10^-1)^(1/2)=10^-1/2>0 -> -1/2.
f / е: sqrt10/100=10^(1/2-2)=10^-3/2>0 -> -3/2=-1.5.
g / ж: fourth-root1000/10=10^(3/4-1)=10^-1/4>0 -> -1/4.
h / з: 100/cube-root10=10^(2-1/3)=10^5/3>0 -> 5/3=1 2/3.
i / и: q=sqrt2/fourth-root40>0. q^4=4/40=1/10, so q=10^-1/4 and lg q=-1/4. Positivity selects the positive fourth root.
All nine asserted source equalities are mathematically correct.

## 734, twelve common logarithms

a / а: lg100=lg10^2=2.
b / б: lg1000000=lg10^6=6.
c / в: lg10^9=9.
d / г: lg0.0001=lg10^-4=-4.
e / д: lg10^-7=-7.
f / е: lg(sqrt10)=1/2.
g / ж: lg(cube-root100)=lg10^(2/3)=2/3.
h / з: lg(fourth-root0.1)=lg10^-1/4=-1/4.
i / и: lg(eighth-root0.01)=lg10^(-2/8)=-1/4. Use the actual source index 8, not the frozen observer's corrected misread 6.
j / к: lg10^(-3/8)=-3/8.
k / л: lg(0.1sqrt10)=lg10^(-1+1/2)=-1/2.
l / м: lg(cube-root100/1000)=lg10^(2/3-3)=-7/3.
All twelve full original arguments are strictly positive.

## 735, eight real equations

Original domain x>0 for every subpart. Injectivity of lg gives exactly one solution x=10^t for lg x=t; all solutions listed lie in that domain.
a / а: t=1 -> x=10.
b / б: t=-3 -> x=10^-3=0.001.
c / в: t=1/2 -> x=sqrt10.
d / г: t=-1/2 -> x=1/sqrt10.
e / д: t=-2/3 -> x=10^-2/3=1/cube-root100=cube-root0.01.
f / е: t=2.5 -> x=10^(5/2)=100sqrt10.
g / ж: t=0 -> x=1.
h / з: t=-0.25 -> x=10^-1/4=1/fourth-root10.
No negative or zero solution admitted.

## 736, nine meaningfulness judgments, with signs/values

The printed argument powers are parsed before lg; the minus in c and g is outside lg.
a / а: lg0.43 is defined, since 0.43>0. Value lg(43/100)<0.
b / б: lg(-10) is undefined over R, since -10<0.
c / в: -lg(1/2) is defined, since 1/2>0; value lg2>0.
d / г: lg((-6)^-6) is defined: (-6)^-6=1/46656>0. Value -6lg6<0; this is NOT (lg(-6))^-6.
e / д: lg((-2.5)^45) is undefined: odd power of negative base is negative.
f / е: lg(5^2.5) is defined: 5^2.5=25sqrt5>0; value (5/2)lg5>0.
g / ж: -lg(0.2^0.5) is defined: sqrt0.2>0; value -(1/2)lg0.2=(1/2)lg5>0.
h / з: lg(2sqrt3-3sqrt2) is undefined. Both positive comparison terms can be squared: (2sqrt3)^2=12<18=(3sqrt2)^2, so the whole argument is negative.
i / и: lg(sqrt2-cube-root3) is undefined. Both positive terms can be raised to the sixth power: (sqrt2)^6=8<9=(cube-root3)^6, so the argument is negative. Do not confuse cube-root3 with sqrt3 or reverse the sign.
Ordered defined flags: true,false,true,true,false,true,true,false,false.

## 737, twelve full original real domains

a / а: 3x>0 -> x>0 -> (0,infinity).
b / б: x/10>0 -> x>0 -> (0,infinity).
c / в: |x|>0 -> x!=0 -> (-infinity,0) union (0,infinity).
d / г: 10+x>0 -> x>-10 -> (-10,infinity).
e / д: x-5>0 -> x>5 -> (5,infinity).
f / е: (x-2)/5>0 -> x>2 -> (2,infinity).
g / ж: 1/(100-x)>0 requires 100-x>0 (and nonzero) -> x<100 -> (-infinity,100).
h / з: x^2>0 -> x!=0 -> (-infinity,0) union (0,infinity). lg(x^2), not (lg x)^2; negative x allowed.
i / и: x^2+1>=1>0 -> all R -> (-infinity,infinity).
j / к: (x-1)/(10-x)>0 with x!=10. Critical values 1,10. For x<1 quotient negative; for 1<x<10 positive; for x>10 negative. Domain (1,10), both endpoints excluded.
k / л: 9-x^2>0 -> x^2<9 -> (-3,3), strict.
l / м: x^2-x=x(x-1)>0 -> x<0 or x>1 -> (-infinity,0) union (1,infinity), strict at both zeroes.
Every union is part of one subpart's domain, not alternative answers. No endpoint with zero logarithm argument is included.

## 738, twelve exponential values

All log arguments here are positive constants. Use 10^(lg b)=b, 10^(u+v)=10^u*10^v, and 10^(u-v)=10^u/10^v.
a / а: 10^(lg1000)=1000.
b / б: 10^(lg100000)=100000.
c / в: 10^(lg0.01)=0.01.
d / г: 10^(lg2)=2.
e / д: 10^(lg0.3)=0.3.
f / е: 10^(1+lg8)=10*8=80.
g / ж: 10^(2+lg0.05)=100*0.05=5.
h / з: 10^(lg3-lg2)=3/2.
i / и: 10^(-lg4)=1/4.
j / к: 10^(-lg0.8)=1/0.8=5/4.
k / л: 10^(2lg3)=(10^(lg3))^2=9.
l / м: 10^((1/2)lg16)=sqrt(10^(lg16))=sqrt16=4.
No exponent's scope shortened; in particular f,g contain the complete sums and l the full (1/2) factor.

## 739, five exact representations as powers of 10

All inputs positive, so exact exponent lg b exists and is unique.
a / а: sqrt1000=(10^3)^(1/2)=10^(3/2).
b / б: 7=10^(lg7).
c / в: 34=10^(lg34).
d / г: 3.2=10^(lg3.2).
e / д: 0.665=10^(lg0.665).
These are exact powers, not rounded decimal exponents. In b-d exponent is positive, e exponent negative; the original decimal 0.665 is not 0.66 or 0.65.

## 740, both graph pairs, full domains, ranges and endpoint data

a / а:
First y=x has domain R, range R, the complete straight line through (-1,-1),(0,0),(1,1).
Second y=10^(lg x) first requires x>0; equals x there. Domain (0,infinity), range (0,infinity). Graph is only the positive part of that straight line, with the origin excluded and approached as x->0+. Example included points (0.1,0.1),(1,1),(10,10). Limit endpoint (0,0) is open, not an included point. No negative half-line and no x=0 can be restored by simplification.

b / б:
First y=x^2 has domain R, range [0,infinity), complete parabola through (-2,4),(-1,1),(0,0),(1,1),(2,4), included vertex (0,0).
Second y=10^(lg(x^2)) first requires x^2>0, i.e. x!=0. Equals x^2 on (-infinity,0) union (0,infinity); range (0,infinity).
Graph is both left and right parabola branches with ONLY (0,0) removed; (-2,4),(-1,1),(1,1),(2,4) included. Both branches approach the open hole (0,0) as x->0- and x->0+. Negative x are allowed. Do not make the second domain x>0, fill the hole, or interpret its exponent as (lg x)^2.
These are independent mathematical graph specifications, not a renderer run or image approval. No new figure generated.

## 741, unrestricted quadratic and its inverse relation

f(x)=x^2+5 with D_f=R. Since x^2>=0 and every t>=0 is attained, range(f)=[5,infinity), endpoint 5 included at x=0.
Interchange input/output in y=x^2+5: relation g is x=y^2+5, equivalently y^2=x-5 or y=+sqrt(x-5) OR y=-sqrt(x-5).
D_g=[5,infinity); range(g)=R. At x=5 both branches meet y=0, included. At x>5 two distinct outputs occur, e.g. x=6 gives y=+1 and -1. Hence g is NOT a single-valued inverse function on this entire domain. Giving only the positive square-root branch or restricting the source f domain is incorrect.
The equation x=y^2+5 compactly includes both branches. Source asks for 相反关系 and imposes no x>=0 restriction.

## 742, both literal rational expressions

a / а:
E(x)=(x/(x-5)+4/(x+4))*(x+4)/(x+10)-3/(x-5).
Original denominators: x-5, x+4, x+10; full original domain R minus {-10,-4,5}.
On precisely that domain,
x/(x-5)+4/(x+4)
 = [x(x+4)+4(x-5)]/[(x-5)(x+4)]
 = (x^2+8x-20)/[(x-5)(x+4)]
 = (x+10)(x-2)/[(x-5)(x+4)].
Multiply by (x+4)/(x+10) to obtain (x-2)/(x-5); subtract 3/(x-5) to obtain (x-5)/(x-5)=1.
Constant 1 only on the ORIGINAL domain; x=-10,-4,5 stay excluded despite cancellations.

b / б, use the complete printed scope without changing grouping:
F(a)=(a-13)/(2a-10)+(a+5)/(a+6)*(a/(a-5)+6/(25-a^2)).
Original denominators: 2a-10, a+6, a-5,25-a^2. Full original domain R minus {-6,-5,5}.
The first fraction is a separate summand; it is not inside the multiplication by the big parentheses.
On this original domain,
25-a^2=-(a-5)(a+5),
a/(a-5)+6/(25-a^2)
 = [a(a+5)-6]/[(a-5)(a+5)]
 = (a^2+5a-6)/[(a-5)(a+5)]
 = (a+6)(a-1)/[(a-5)(a+5)].
Multiplying this last value by (a+5)/(a+6) gives (a-1)/(a-5).
Then
F(a)=(a-13)/[2(a-5)]+(a-1)/(a-5)
 = (3a-15)/[2(a-5)]
 = 3/2.
The result 3/2 is established by the actual expression, not guessed from the heading. All three original exclusions -6,-5,5 remain. a=0 and a=1 are allowed and each gives 3/2; the cancellation of a+6 and a+5 does not make -6 or -5 admissible.
Both constant claims are mathematically correct as printed. Confirmed source mathematical errata: 0. Do not alter the author or source.

